# Copy to config.env (gitignored) and edit. Both the server and the bash
# scripts read this file, so each value is defined exactly once.
#   cp config.example.env config.env
#
# It is deliberately shell-sourceable:  source config.env

# --- server ---
# Loopback only. This server opens shells, so it must never bind 0.0.0.0.
CV_HOST=127.0.0.1
CV_PORT=8788

# --- local terminals ---
# Directory a new terminal starts in. Defaults to $HOME.
# CV_DEFAULT_CWD=~/repos
# CV_DEFAULT_SHELL=/bin/zsh

# --- remote hosts ---
# Any number, each a numbered slot. _ID and _SSH_TARGET are required; a slot
# missing either is ignored with a warning rather than silently. The id is what
# sessions and presets record, so renaming one orphans its saved sessions.
#
# A host declared here survives a fresh clone and is the one to use for
# anything permanent. For "I have a second box, let me point at it right now"
# there is also the Hosts button in the running viewer: it adds a remote with
# no restart and no file editing, kept in .state/hosts.json (gitignored, like
# this file). Either way ends up the same: a RemoteConfig with the same
# defaults, so nothing here is special to hand-editing.
#
# CV_HOST_1_ID=fire
# CV_HOST_1_SSH_TARGET=user@10.0.0.1
# CV_HOST_1_KEY_PATH=~/.ssh/your-key
#   Absolute path to claude on that box. It is usually not on PATH for a
#   non-interactive shell, where a bare `claude` fails silently.
# CV_HOST_1_CLAUDE_PATH=$HOME/.local/bin/claude
#   Model for every Claude session started on this host, unless a spawn asks
#   for another. This is how "everything on this box is sonnet" becomes a fact
#   about the host rather than something each caller has to remember. The model
#   a session actually started with is shown on its node.
# CV_HOST_1_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#   Only for a host fire-control can start and stop. A host without an
#   instance id simply has no instance light, which is correct.
# CV_HOST_1_INSTANCE_ID=i-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# CV_HOST_1_API_BASE=http://fire-control/api
# CV_HOST_1_LABEL=fire (dev box)
#
# CV_HOST_2_ID=gpu-box
# CV_HOST_2_SSH_TARGET=user@gpu.internal
#
# The ControlMaster socket defaults to ~/.ssh/cv-<id>-%r@%h:%p — one per host,
# because sharing a socket sends the second host's commands down the first
# host's connection. Override only if you know why.
# CV_HOST_1_CONTROL_PATH=~/.ssh/cv-fire-%r@%h:%p
#
# Tip: if the target is a Host alias in ~/.ssh/config, then ProxyJump, bastions,
# IdentityFile and per-host User all apply for free and KEY_PATH is unnecessary.

# --- older single-host keys ---
# Still supported, and mean a host whose id is "fire". An explicit
# CV_HOST_n_ID=fire takes precedence, so the two cannot conflict.
# CV_FIRE_INSTANCE_ID=i-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# CV_FIRE_SSH_TARGET=user@10.0.0.1
# CV_FIRE_KEY_PATH=~/.ssh/your-key
# CV_FIRE_API_BASE=http://fire-control/api
